# Write Comments and Docs for the General Case

When writing code comments, doc strings, or contract documentation (e.g. `docs/indexer-contract.md`), describe what the code or field **is** — not what one specific consumer does with it, and not the ticket that motivated it.

**Rule:** If your description would only make sense for a single caller, a single feature, or a specific Jira ticket, drop that context and write for the general case.

**Wrong:**
```
// committee:{uid} — filters messages for the weekly brief; only present when the list has a committee association
```

**Right:**
```
// committee:{uid} — only present when the list has a committee association
```

**Also wrong:**
```
// Added for LFXV2-3048 to support the committee service
```

**Right:** Put ticket context in the commit message or PR description — not in the code or docs.
